# Privacy remediation working files must never be committed —
# they contain the private tokens they exist to remove.
.sanitize-map.txt
# The guard's own hostname list. It enumerates the private TLDs verbatim, so
# committing it publishes exactly the naming scheme the guard exists to hide.
# The content-scanning guards do NOT catch it: they match hostname shape
# (label.tld) and this file holds bare TLDs, so it reads clean to both the
# pre-commit hook and CI. This line is the only thing keeping it out —
# tests/unit/test_no_private_infrastructure.py asserts that it still works.
.privacy-local
